GeneralsX: FSR 3 frame generation, DXVK_FSR3_FRAMEGEN=1 with
DXVK_UPSCALER=fsr3. Uses the FidelityFX optical flow and frame
interpolation effects directly, not the SDK's swap chain replacement: the
frame is interpolated between the previous and the current upscaled 3D
scene, then the composite pass draws the interface of the current, real
frame over it, so the interface is never interpolated. The D3D9 swap chain
presents each frame twice, the generated frame first and then the real
one; the real frame is presented half a frame interval later
(DXVK_FSR3_FRAMEGEN_PACING=0 turns this off). Frame generation is turned
off with an [FSR3] log line when a frame latency tracker is active or the
swap chain has fewer than 3 images. DXVK_FSR3_DEBUG=tearlines, view or
resets shows the FidelityFX debug overlays.

